{%- comment -%}
  Rendered once inside <head> of layout/theme.liquid (and password.liquid),
  AFTER both Dawn (@layer dawn) and Webflow (@layer webflow) stylesheet
  loads. Anything emitted here is "outside" both layers — so it has higher
  precedence than ANY layered rule (per CSS cascade-layer spec).

  Currently emits merchant-pasted Custom CSS. Useful for harmonizing the
  visual seam between brand (Webflow) and commerce (Dawn) pages: paste
  brand-color overrides, font-family unification, spacing tweaks, etc.

  If you later want merchant-controlled brand colors / font scale / layout
  toggles, add :root { --var: {{ settings.X }}; } blocks here and the
  matching settings to config/settings_schema.json. Keep the
  `{% if settings.X != blank %}` guard so empty settings never override
  the design's defaults.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if settings.custom_css != blank -%}
<style id="theme-custom-css">
{{ settings.custom_css }}
</style>
{%- endif -%}
